# npm package installation

When installing npm packages, always install the latest version by appending `@latest` and target the right workspace with `--filter`.

Examples:

```bash
pnpm add some-package@latest --filter @raadmounif/web
pnpm add -D some-types@latest --filter @raadmounif/web
pnpm add some-server-package@latest --filter @raadmounif/api
```

Never install runtime deps in the workspace root. The root `package.json` is dev-only (turbo, prettier, husky, etc.).
